NOTES
- Page root: every section element carries the class `lm-fj` (the page-root
  scope) in addition to its own wrapper class. The master.css is scoped under
  `.lm-fj`, so this class must be present on each Custom HTML element for the
  styles to apply.
- master.css and master.js are stored here EXACTLY as they are pasted into
  Ontraport, including their surrounding `<style>` and `<script>` tags. This
  differs from member-portal-during, whose master.css has no wrapper tag. They
  are kept verbatim so the file can be pasted back without editing.
  master.css -> page Header Code.  master.js -> page Footer Code.
- design-system.css is not hand-maintained. It is the prefix of master.css --
  everything before the "SECTION 1 -- NAVIGATION" header, i.e. the canonical
  Ontraport-hosted fonts, the `:root` tokens and the global typography. It is
  extracted for reference only; master.css remains the file that ships.
- Merge fields: Ontraport resolves `[Page//Field]` merges BOTH in text nodes and
  inside HTML attributes on this page (an href merge resolves correctly -- see
  the Things To Do card). Some older comments in these files claim attributes
  are never merged; that is wrong. The hidden `.lm-fj-mf` merge feed is kept as
  a belt-and-braces channel for values the JS needs to read.
- The page object is Registrations (Ontraport object 10001), so `[Page//...]`
  resolves against a registration, and `[Page//Contact//...]` hops to its
  contact. NB the registration's `unique_id` and the contact's `unique_id` are
  different values -- the journey URL uses the contact's, the confirmation page
  URL uses the registration's. Do not hand-build these URLs; merge the stored
  field instead.

