SECTION 3 -- INFORMATION FORM TWO-STATE CARD

The third card in Things To Do has two states, driven by the registration's
"Information Form Completed" checkbox (field f2579 on object 10001).

How it works:
- The value reaches the page through the hidden merge feed span
  `<span class="lm-fj-mf" data-mf="infodone">[Page//Information Form Completed]`.
- It is a checkbox field, and it merges as the WORD "Yes" (not 1/0). The
  unchecked counterpart is "No" or empty.
- master.js matches against an allowlist (yes/y/1/true/on/checked/complete/
  completed). The allowlist is deliberate: an unrecognised value falls through
  to "incomplete", which shows the call-to-action to someone who may have
  already filled the form. That is a harmless annoyance. Falling through the
  other way would hide the CTA from someone who has not filled it, and the
  details would never arrive.
- Incomplete copy is the visible text in the HTML. Completed copy lives in the
  `data-done-*` attributes on the card, so both states are editable in one
  place. The JS swaps one for the other and caches the authored copy so
  repeated runs are idempotent.
- When complete the card stops being a link (`removeAttribute("href")`) and the
  action label is hidden in CSS. The card otherwise keeps the same teal, coral
  left border and full-colour photo as its two neighbours.
- The pill holds an inline SVG checkmark plus a separate label span. The label
  is what the JS swaps -- setting textContent on the pill itself would delete
  the icon.

The card's link is `[Page//Registration Confirmation URL]` (field page_112_url),
merged straight into the href. The JS deliberately contains NO url handling --
see "Ontraport custom-code sanitizer" below.

