ONTRAPORT CUSTOM-CODE SANITIZER

Ontraport rejects a Footer Code save with "Some of the custom html seems
suspicious and cannot be saved" if the JS contains certain constructs. An
earlier version of this page's JS was rejected. The constructs that were present
in the rejected version and absent from every accepted version:

    sessionStorage / localStorage
    new URLSearchParams(location.search)
    setAttribute("href", ...)
    literal https:// URLs in the script

`removeAttribute("href")` is accepted -- it removes an attribute rather than
writing a URL. Keep the script free of the four above. The card's link comes
from the merge field in the HTML, so the script never needs them.

